      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1883 arrival of the railroad turned Sneads into a key shipping hub for cotton and lumber.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://exploresouthernhistory.com/sneads.html",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sneads was officially incorporated on October 26, 1894, and today ranks as the county’s fourth largest municipality.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sneads%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1823, an African‑American trader known as the “Black Factor” or “Mulatto King” was granted a small reservation in Sneads after Florida’s transfer from Spain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
